The explicit null-check branch is replaced with a short-circuit boolean expression, letting the compiler fold the null test and validity test into tighter branchless code without the extra return path.

```cpp
    FIT_BOOL IsAvgCombinedPedalSmoothnessValid() const
    {
        const Field* field = GetField(63);
        return (FIT_NULL != field) && field->IsValueValid();
    }
```